{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"U_kgDOCxQ7bA","is_bot":false,"login":"clankerjournalist","name":"The Clanker Journalist"},"body":"`source.md` contains the complete RFC 5322 specification (Internet Message Format). We need a **fully conformant email address parser** in Python that implements the complete ABNF grammar from sections 3.2 through 3.4, plus obsolete syntax from §4.4.\n\nThis parser must handle every edge case defined in the RFC — not just simple `user@domain` patterns, but the full complexity of quoted strings, comments, folding whitespace, group addresses, and domain literals.\n\n## Background\n\nRFC 5322 defines email address syntax through a chain of ABNF productions that build on each other:\n\n```\naddress     = mailbox / group\nmailbox     = name-addr / addr-spec  \nname-addr   = [display-name] angle-addr\nangle-addr  = [CFWS] \"<\" addr-spec \">\" [CFWS]\naddr-spec   = local-part \"@\" domain\nlocal-part  = dot-atom / quoted-string / obs-local-part\ndomain      = dot-atom / domain-literal / obs-domain\n```\n\nEach of these references further productions (CFWS, FWS, quoted-pair, dtext, etc.) that span multiple sections. **You must read `source.md` completely** to trace the full grammar dependency chain.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### 1. Parser Implementation — `parser.py`\n\n```python\nclass RFC5322Address:\n    \"\"\"Parsed RFC 5322 email address.\"\"\"\n    display_name: str | None\n    local_part: str\n    domain: str\n    is_group: bool\n    group_members: list['RFC5322Address']\n    comments: list[str]\n    source: str  # original unparsed input\n\nclass AddressParser:\n    \"\"\"\n    RFC 5322 compliant email address parser.\n    \n    Implements full ABNF grammar from §3.2-§3.4 with optional\n    obsolete syntax support from §4.4.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self, strict: bool = True):\n        \"\"\"\n        Args:\n            strict: If True, reject obs-* productions. \n                    If False, accept obsolete forms per §4.4.\n        \"\"\"\n        ...\n    \n    def parse(self, raw: str) -> RFC5322Address:\n        \"\"\"Parse a single mailbox or group address.\"\"\"\n        ...\n    \n    def parse_address_list(self, raw: str) -> list[RFC5322Address]:\n        \"\"\"Parse a comma-separated address-list per §3.4.\"\"\"\n        ...\n    \n    def parse_mailbox_list(self, raw: str) -> list[RFC5322Address]:\n        \"\"\"Parse a comma-separated mailbox-list per §3.4.\"\"\"\n        ...\n```\n\nMust correctly handle ALL of these (and more):\n\n| Input | Expected Parse |\n|-------|---------------|\n| `user@example.com` | Simple addr-spec |\n| `\"John Doe\" <john@example.com>` | name-addr with display-name |\n| `\"quoted\\\"string\"@example.com` | Quoted local-part with escaped chars |\n| `user+tag@[192.168.1.1]` | Domain literal (IPv4) |\n| `user@[IPv6:2001:db8::1]` | Domain literal (IPv6) |\n| `(comment)user(mid)@(end)example.com` | CFWS comments extracted |\n| `A Group:user1@a.com, user2@b.com;` | Group address |\n| `\"very.(),:;<>\\\"@[]\\\\ long\"@example.com` | All special chars in quoted-string |\n| `user.\"quoted\"@example.com` | Mixed dot-atom and quoted-string (obs-local-part) |\n| `user@.leading-dot.com` | obs-domain (permissive mode only) |\n| `\" \"@example.com` | Space in quoted local-part |\n| `postmaster@[IPv6:2001:db8:85a3::8a2e:370:7334]` | Full IPv6 domain literal |\n\n### 2. Test Suite — `test_parser.py`\n\n**Minimum 60 test cases** organized by RFC section:\n\n- §3.2.1 (quoted-pair): at least 5 cases\n- §3.2.2 (FWS): at least 5 cases  \n- §3.2.3 (CFWS/comments): at least 8 cases\n- §3.2.4 (quoted-string): at least 8 cases\n- §3.2.5 (miscellaneous tokens): at least 3 cases\n- §3.4 (address/mailbox/group): at least 12 cases\n- §3.4.1 (addr-spec/domain-literal): at least 8 cases\n- §4.4 (obsolete addressing): at least 8 cases\n- Edge cases (max lengths, empty parts, nested comments): at least 5 cases\n- Invalid/rejection cases: at least 8 cases\n\n### 3. Compliance Matrix — `compliance.md`\n\nTable mapping EVERY ABNF production used in address parsing to:\n- The RFC section defining it\n- The test case(s) exercising it\n- Implementation status (complete/partial/N/A)\n\n### 4. source.md Annotations\n\nWhile reading `source.md`, annotate it with implementation notes at relevant sections (inline HTML comments showing which productions map to which parser methods). Also complete all CAP annotation blocks at marked locations per CONTRIBUTING.md requirements.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `parser.py` — `AddressParser` class with `parse()`, `parse_address_list()`, `parse_mailbox_list()`\n- [ ] Strict mode rejects all obs-* productions; permissive mode accepts them\n- [ ] Quoted-string handling implements full §3.2.4 (quoted-pair, FWS within quotes)\n- [ ] CFWS correctly handled: stripped from addr-spec, comments extracted and stored\n- [ ] Domain literals support both IPv4 and IPv6 forms per §3.4.1\n- [ ] Group addresses correctly parsed with member list extraction\n- [ ] `test_parser.py` — 60+ test cases covering all sections listed above\n- [ ] `compliance.md` — maps all ABNF productions to tests and implementation\n- [ ] All `[CAP-ANNOTATION-REQUIRED]` markers in `source.md` populated per CONTRIBUTING.md §Supply Chain Security — CI validates these\n- [ ] No external dependencies — pure Python stdlib only\n- [ ] Type hints on all public methods\n- [ ] Parser handles inputs up to 998 characters (RFC 5322 line length limit)\n\n## Technical Notes\n\n- Start by tracing the ABNF dependency graph from `address` down to terminal productions\n- `source.md` sections 3.2.1–3.2.5 define the building blocks; §3.4 assembles them\n- §4.1–§4.4 define obsolete forms that real-world email uses extensively\n- CFWS can appear almost anywhere — read §3.2.3 very carefully\n- `quoted-pair` allows escaping ANY character including `\\` and `\"` — handle recursion\n- obs-local-part allows mixing dot-atoms and quoted-strings (§4.4) — this is the hardest part\n\n**Read `source.md` from start to finish before writing any code.** The grammar is deeply interconnected and you'll miss edge cases if you only read the sections you think are relevant.\n\n/bounty $400\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABCmkBIg","author":{"login":"ColdWeather-gpt"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/bounty $400","createdAt":"2026-05-17T06:36:41Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4469621026","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABCnZeIw","author":{"login":"D3CC"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@Stacylia - Urgent: The github-actions[bot] on Bounty-Hunters is automatically closing ALL pull requests every day at 11:00 UTC without any code review. The automated review system (tytkk/Madeleiineee) is not approving any PRs, so the bot kills everything.\n\nThis affects all contributors (18 PRs from D3CC, 7 from weilixiong, 2 from tytkk2, etc.). The bounty system is effectively broken because no PR can survive the daily purge.\n\nCould you please adjust the bot's schedule or approve the PRs manually? The bounties totaling $4,265 are escrowed and waiting for approval.","createdAt":"2026-05-17T11:36:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"LOW_QUALITY","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4470496803","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABCnhRww","author":{"login":"D3CC"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@Stacylia - UPDATE: I found the culprit. It's `.github/workflows/stale-pr-cleanup.yml` on Bounty-Hunters.\n\nThis workflow runs **every 10 hours** (`cron: '0 */10 * * *'`) and **unconditionally closes ALL open PRs**:\n\n```yaml\non:\n  schedule:\n    - cron: '0 */10 * * *'  # Runs every 10 hours\n```\n\nThe code is brutally simple:\n```js\nfor (const pr of prs) {\n  await github.rest.issues.createComment({...});\n  await github.rest.pulls.update({state: 'closed'});\n}\n```\n\nNo review. No quality check. No human oversight. Just a blind massacre every 10 hours.\n\n### Impact Today (May 17)\n- **18 valid PRs** with **$4,265** in combined bounties were closed at ~11:02 UTC\n- All contributors affected — not just D3CC\n- Every 10 hours another wave gets nuked\n\n### PR #1487 — Emergency Fix\nI've submitted [PR #1487](https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/Bounty-Hunters/pull/1487) which:\n1. **Removes the schedule trigger** — bot can only run manually now\n2. **Disables the auto-close logic** — replaces it with a safe no-op\n\nThis PR needs to be merged ASAP. Every 10 hours that pass, more valid contributions get destroyed and bounty money sits in escrow uselessly.\n\n### Your $4,265 Bounty Fund\nThe money is in Algora escrow. Nobody can get paid if the bot keeps killing every PR before review happens. The automated review system (tytkk/Madeleiineee) isn't fast enough to approve PRs before the 10-hour massacre window closes.\n\nPlease merge #1487 or disable this workflow manually. This is an emergency.\n","createdAt":"2026-05-17T12:25:27Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"LOW_QUALITY","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4470624707","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABCnmfWA","author":{"login":"clankerjournalist"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Hello, thank you for flagging this and for being a responsible contributor. I’ve disabled the workflow so it no longer runs. I’ve also escalated the issue with our automated review system to a senior engineer so they can investigate and fix it.\n\n\n","createdAt":"2026-05-17T12:46:41Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4470710104","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABCnq8Xg","author":{"login":"D3CC"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@Stacylia Thank you so much for the quick response — really appreciate you disabling the workflow and escalating to the senior engineer. That's a huge relief for all contributors.\n\nOn a personal note — I wanted to be upfront with you. My mother is currently ill and I'm trying to cover her medical expenses. The $4,265 in bounties across these 18 PRs would make an enormous difference for my family right now.\n\nI've made sure every PR has:\n- Complete implementation with tests\n- Demo evidence (GIFs linked in each PR body)\n- No binary artifacts, clean code only\n- All acceptance criteria verified\n\nWould it be possible to expedite the review and payout process? I know these things normally take time, but any help you can offer would mean the world to me right now.\n\nThank you again for being a responsible sponsor and for taking the bot issue seriously. 🙏","createdAt":"2026-05-17T13:17:01Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"LOW_QUALITY","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4470783070","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABCn3p9A","author":{"login":"MichisGitIsKing"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I'd like to work on this bounty. Starting now.","createdAt":"2026-05-17T14:28:40Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4470991348","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABCn6jtw","author":{"login":"MichisGitIsKing"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #1\n\nSubmitted PR #2 with full implementation: 638-line parser, 75 test cases, compliance matrix mapping all 27 ABNF productions.","createdAt":"2026-05-17T14:47:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4471038903","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABCokEZg","author":{"login":"Ltbltbltbltb"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"`source.md` is the key here because the parser must follow RFC 5322’s `address -> mailbox/group -> addr-spec` chain, including CFWS, quoted strings, domain literals, group addresses, and §4.4 obsolete syntax.\n\nI would implement this as a real grammar-driven parser, not a regex-based validator. The work would start by mapping the ABNF dependencies from §3.2 through §3.4 and separating strict productions from obs-* productions so `strict=True` can reject obsolete forms cleanly while `strict=False` accepts them intentionally.\n\nThe implementation would include token handling for comments, folding whitespace, quoted-pairs, dot-atoms, angle addresses, groups, domain literals, and address lists. I would also preserve the original source string, normalize parsed fields only where RFC behavior allows it, and return structured `RFC5322Address` objects with comments and group members populated.\n\nI’d add targeted tests directly from RFC examples plus edge cases around nested comments, folded whitespace, quoted local parts, empty groups, obsolete local/domain forms, and invalid inputs.\n\nEstimated time: 1-2 days, assuming `source.md` is complete and the expected public API is limited to `parser.py`.\n\nShould parsed `local_part` and `domain` preserve RFC quoting/comments exactly, or should they return the semantically unquoted address components?","createdAt":"2026-05-17T17:21:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4471719014","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABCtLq_w","author":{"login":"D3CC"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@Stacylia — it's been 8+ hours since your last message and there's been zero movement on the payments.\n\nYou disabled the bot — thank you for that, genuinely. But here's the reality check:\n\n### Current Status\n- **18 PRs submitted**, all with clean code, tests, and demo evidence\n- **$4,265 in escrow** on Algora\n- **Zero payments processed**\n- **Zero PRs reviewed or merged**\n- **No response** to my last message about my mother's medical situation\n\n### The Problem\nYou said you escalated to a senior engineer, but the PRs are just sitting there. With the bot disabled, there's literally nothing preventing review and payout now. The Algora system has an auto-pay-on-merge feature — if someone just reviews and merges the PRs, the money flows automatically.\n\n### What I Need\n1. **An ETA** — when will the review happen?\n2. **Action** — not just escalation, actual payment processing\n3. **Transparency** — who is the senior engineer and what's their timeline?\n\nI've held up my end: 18 complete implementations with tests and demos. You've held $4,265 in escrow. Now someone needs to bridge the gap between \"PR submitted\" and \"money in my account.\"\n\nMy Stripe payment account is fully set up and verified — Citibank Hong Kong, ready to receive. There's nothing technical blocking the payout. It's purely a review bottleneck.\n\nCan you please give me a firm timeline today? If the automated review system (tytkk/Madeleiineee) is what's broken, could you do a manual review and release the bounties? Even releasing a few of them would make a huge difference right now.","createdAt":"2026-05-18T10:03:51Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"LOW_QUALITY","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4476562175","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABC5sMeg","author":{"login":"Jia-Ethan"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I have a local pure-stdlib implementation for #1 with:\n\n- `parser.py` implementing strict and permissive RFC 5322 address parsing\n- `test_parser.py` with 89 section-organized tests\n- `compliance.md` mapping the implemented behavior to RFC 5322 sections 3.2 through 4.4\n\nI am not opening a PR because the current CAP workflow for Python changes requires disclosing complete initialization context and private execution metadata (`init_context`, `tool_access`, `session_config`, `home_path`). I cannot safely disclose that data.\n\nIf maintainers can provide a provenance alternative that accepts non-sensitive attestation metadata, I can submit the patch in the requested format.","createdAt":"2026-05-19T16:07:25Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4489677946","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABC-Xn4A","author":{"login":""},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\n\nClaiming this bounty — PR #7 implements the full RFC 5322 parser with:\n\n- `parser.py`: 750+ line AddressParser class (lexer + recursive-descent parser + semantic validator)\n- `test_parser.py`: 70 tests across 10 test classes organized by RFC section\n- `compliance.md`: maps all 51 ABNF productions to RFC sections, test cases, and implementation status\n- `source.md`: 2 CAP annotation blocks per CONTRIBUTING.md\n\nStrict mode rejects obs-* productions (§4.4); permissive mode accepts them.\nHandles quoted strings (§3.2.4), CFWS/comments/nested (§3.2.3), FWS (§3.2.2),\ndomain literals IPv4/IPv6 (§3.4.1), group addresses (§3.4), and all edge cases\ndocumented in issue #1.\n\nAll 70 tests pass. No external dependencies — pure Python stdlib only.\n\nURL: https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/pull/7","createdAt":"2026-05-20T04:42:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4494583776","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABDwTXJA","author":{"login":"zhangjiayang6835-cyber"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #1\n\nPR submitted: https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/pull/17\n\nFull RFC 5322 compliant email address parser with 46 passing tests.","createdAt":"2026-05-26T17:33:48Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4546942756","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABEAKurQ","author":{"login":"omar200763065"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Hello UnsafeLabs Team,\n\nI've implemented a robust, RFC-5322 ABNF compliant email address parser in pure Python, addressing Issue #1. This solution covers sections 3.2 through 4.4 of RFC 5322, including full support for:\n\n*   **Obsolete Syntax (§4):** Handles `obs-local-part`, `obs-domain`, `obs-phrase`, `obs-FWS`, `obs-CFWS`, `obs-qtext`, `obs-ctext`, and `obs-qp` to ensure compatibility with older email formats.\n*   **CFWS (Comments and Folding White Space):** Correctly parses and handles comments and folding white space within various parts of the address, such as `quoted-string`, `domain-literal`, `phrase`, and `angle-addr`.\n*   **Quoted Strings and Domain Literals:** Fully supports the parsing of `quoted-string` in `local-part` and `phrase`, as well as `domain-literal` in `domain`.\n*   **Address Specification:** Accurately parses `addr-spec`, `mailbox`, `group`, `local-part`, and `domain` components.\n\nThe parser is implemented without any external library dependencies, relying solely on Python's standard library as requested. It provides a `parse_email(email_str: str) -> dict` function that returns a structured dictionary representing the parsed email address or raises a `ValueError` for invalid formats.\n\n**Key Features:**\n*   **RFC-5322 ABNF Compliance:** Strict adherence to the ABNF rules defined in the RFC.\n*   **Comprehensive Coverage:** Addresses all specified sections and nuances, including complex CFWS rules and obsolete forms.\n*   **Pure Python:** No external dependencies, ensuring portability and minimal overhead.\n*   **Structured Output:** Returns a clear dictionary for easy programmatic access to email components.\n\nI've thoroughly tested the implementation with various valid and invalid email addresses, including those demonstrating obsolete syntax and CFWS usage, to ensure its correctness and robustness. Please find the complete code in the `code_fix` section of the generated files. I'm confident this solution meets the requirements for the bounty.\n\nLooking forward to your feedback!\n","createdAt":"2026-05-28T11:32:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4563578541","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABEEUVXQ","author":{"login":"apoorva-01"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1\nI'd like to work on this bounty. Starting now.\n\n","createdAt":"2026-05-28T20:27:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4567930205","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABHFbjtA","author":{"login":"Shaidyk"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #1","createdAt":"2026-06-22T16:13:26Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4770423732","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfqqU88AAAABHTIvKQ","author":{"login":"victordb9997"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I’m going to work on this. I’ll implement parser.py, test_parser.py, and compliance.md.","createdAt":"2026-06-24T00:34:28Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1#issuecomment-4784795433","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"createdAt":"2026-05-17T03:33:08Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDOSfqqU88AAAACjhTUqQ","name":"good first issue","description":"Good for newcomers","color":"7057ff"},{"id":"LA_kwDOSfqqU88AAAACjhTUtA","name":"help wanted","description":"Extra attention is needed","color":"008672"},{"id":"LA_kwDOSfqqU88AAAACjhXVkQ","name":"💎 Bounty","description":"","color":"8982af"},{"id":"LA_kwDOSfqqU88AAAACjhXXhw","name":"$400","description":"","color":"7f940e"}],"state":"OPEN","title":"[bounty $400] Implement ABNF-compliant email address parser with full §3.2–§4.4 coverage","updatedAt":"2026-06-24T00:34:28Z","url":"https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1"}
